CHAPTER.VERS:
Hear diligently my speech; And let this be your

          {+}
         consolations.

Mark me, and be astonished, And lay your

          {+}
         hand on your

          {+}
         mouth.

[You

          {+}
         say], God lays up his iniquity for his sons. Let him recompense it to himself, that he may know it:

Look, I know your

          {+}
         thoughts, And the devices with which you

          {+}
         would wrong me.

For you

          {+}
         say, Where is the house of the prince? And where is the tent in which the wicked dwelt?

Have you

          {+}
         not asked wayfaring men? And don't you

          {+}
         know their evidences,

How then do you

          {+}
         comfort me in vain, Seeing in your

          {+}
         answers there remains [only] falsehood?
